  "steps": [
    "Combine the rinsed dry quinoa and low-sodium chicken broth in a medium saucepan over medium-high heat. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low, cover with a tight-fitting lid, and simmer for 15 minutes until the liquid is fully absorbed and the quinoa is fluffy.",
    "Whisk together 2 tablespoons of olive oil, lemon juice, minced garlic, dried oregano, half of the salt, and half of the black pepper in a medium bowl. Add the diced chicken breasts and toss until thoroughly coated.",
    "Heat the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the marinated chicken pieces in a single layer and cook for 6 to 8 minutes, stirring occasionally, until golden brown and the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C).",
    "Divide the cooked quinoa evenly among 4 meal prep containers. Top each with the cooked lemon herb chicken, diced cucumber, halved cherry tomatoes, and crumbled feta cheese. Seal and store."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Let the chicken and quinoa cool completely before sealing the containers to prevent condensation.",
    "Add the cucumber and tomatoes to a separate small compartment if you prefer to keep them crisp when reheating.",
    "Substitute brown rice for the quinoa if desired."
  ],
  "storage": "Store in airtight containers in the refrigerator for up to 4 days. Do not freeze.",
  "tools": [
